## Repository Structure

The repository is organized into the following sections:

### CW

The CW folder contains the classwork completed during the session. This section represents the practical work carried out as part of the classroom activities and exercises.

### HW

The HW folder contains the assigned homework and related work completed as part of the session requirements.

This separation keeps the academic work organized and makes it easier to identify classwork and homework independently.

## Purpose of the Repository

The primary purpose of this repository is to maintain a digital record of the work completed during Session 8. It provides a structured and accessible way to submit, review, and maintain academic work using GitHub.

Using a repository also helps in developing familiarity with essential version control practices, including organizing files, maintaining revisions, and documenting completed work.

